+# 2.7.19-rc.3 — local audit candidate, not published
+
+- Isolated readiness, ordered choice saves, bounded background preset saves, reference recovery and private pinned dependencies.
+- Measured structured progress, limited per-frame status writes, protected job transitions and verified orphan shutdown.
+- Actual update-lock checks prevent abandoned update flags from blocking Make. Customer release requires exact-version acceptance on both hosts.
+- Complete reference-scan barriers and content-bound reference evidence prevent silent partial styles and late-index invalidation.
+- Legacy activity records use actual writer locks; managed project tools bind to one installation with unrelated native bridges disabled in that process only.
+- Historical verification flags do not certify this candidate. See the local release acceptance gate before packaging.
+
+## 2.7.18 — Exact colour choices and caption control
+
+- Studio Captions On / Off saves per video and in presets. Off preserves the chosen font/style and prevents stale captioned composites being reused. Existing exports remain unchanged until a new edit.
+- Original adds no creative colour filter. Every named look uses an executable pinned recipe; reference colour uses measured current-reference values. The classic renderer uses the same colour contract.
+- Selected effects require attached real slots, not a name-only applied claim. Missing fonts fail explicitly rather than silently substituting another face; font assets with equal filenames keep distinct content.
+- Concurrent videos get distinct folders atomically. Existing projects, preset versions, style code and learning memory remain protected during updates.
+- Verified with synthetic actual colour and caption renders plus regression tests. Individual artistic results and every possible host/security environment cannot be guaranteed.
+
 # 2.7.17 — editor connection and renderer recovery
 
 - Keep Claude and Codex sessions tied to the selected host; preserve the saved exact request across recovery.
