 On Mac, the app supplies sandbox.network.allowLocalBinding only after an explicit human CreatorCut-loopback consent receipt exists in its protected control folder. Never create that receipt yourself or ask for sandbox-off rendering as a substitute. The setting keeps the host sandbox and normal tool rules enabled. Fresh sessions apply it; an idle connection with older scopes is closed before the next requested turn, without interrupting an active writer or replaying old approvals. Missing consent belongs to first-time setup, before Make dispatches a job.
 The owned rendering process uses a private Puppeteer pipe and a single-process browser layout. Optional lowering of its own CPU priority is skipped only when denied; other failures still propagate. Missing boot information produces an invocation-specific unknown cleanup scope; it never fabricates machine uptime or matches another render through a shared unknown value. The private renderer patch is installed during setup/update only, is version checked and preserves the original module. Validation, requested resolution, frame rate, colour settings and review gates stay in force.
+
+For verified footage without an audio stream, `prepare` supplies the real empty transcript automatically. Use normal `plan` (optionally with --ranges JSON) and `cut`. Do not write a custom Python script or fake speech/word data to create this cut. Continue normal composition/review; no audio is a supported source type, not permission to ignore requested effects.
+
